Hunting {{MobSprite|Glacite Walker}}s and {{MobSprite|Ghost}}s grants {{Green|50%}} of the base {{Skill|Hunting|XP}}.

Each dropped shard from [[Hunting]] or [[Charming]] grants {{Skill|Hunting|XP}}.

=== Critter Safari ===
Catching critters with [[Critter Capsule]]s grants the same amount of {{Skill|Hunting|XP}} as normal mob hunting, which can be increased depending on [[Safari Ticket]] tier via {{Stat|Hunting Wisdom}}. After catching certain amount of critters in a biome, player can claim [[Safari Milestones]] to get more {{Skill|Hunting|XP}}. [[Critterdex]] and [[Sparkling Critterdex]] also grant {{Skill|Hunting|XP}}.

Every player also gets {{Skill XP|5,000 Hunting}} per unique caught [[Critter]] on the [[Critter Safari]], maxing out at {{Skill XP|185,000 Hunting}} per instance. 

'''Critter Safari''' [[Floor Drops]] can grant {{Skill XP|2500-10000 Hunting}}.

=== Other ===
Players can also get '''Hunting''' experience from: 
*{{NPCSprite|David Hunterborough}}'s [[David Hunterborough#Trap Hunts|Trap Hunts]] and [[David Hunterborough#Salt Hunts|Salt Hunts]] milestones;
*from {{Coll|Lushlilac 4}}, {{Coll|Tender Wood 8}} and {{Coll|Vinesap 8}} collection tiers;
*and from [[Trapper Animals]].
=== Increasing amount of Hunting XP gained ===
{{Skill|Hunting|XP}} gain can be increased with {{Stat|Hunting Wisdom}}.

Additionally, [[Critters]] grant more {{Skill|Hunting|XP}}, depending on player's [[Bestiary]] tier for that mob.

== Hunting Methods ==
=== Forest Hunting ===
[[Attributes|Forest Attributes]] require an {{Item|Abysmal Lasso}} or better. To hunt with a Lasso, one must cast the [[Lassos|Lasso]] at them and wait for their stamina meter to deplete until '''{{Yellow|REEL}}''' appears. Some mobs, like {{MobSprite|Dreadwing}}s and {{MobSprite|Cinderbat}}s, have multiple stamina bars.

The {{Attr|Hunter's Suppress}} attribute increases how much Lassos deplete a creature's stamina by.

=== Water Hunting ===
[[Attributes|Water Attributes]] require a {{Item|Basic Fishing Net}} or better. Some mobs are caught instantly, like {{MobSprite|Verdant}}s and {{MobSprite|Birries}}, while others have health that is depleted upon being caught. The damage dealt by a [[Fishing Nets|Fishing Net]] is determined by your {{Stat|pull}}.

The {{Attr|Eelastic}} attribute grants increased {{Stat|pull}}.

=== Combat Hunting ===
[[Attributes|Combat Attributes]] require a {{Item|Worn Huntaxe - Genesis}} and {{Item|Small Pocket Black Hole}} or better. Any melee [[Weapons|Weapon]] can be inserted into a [[Huntaxes|huntaxe]] to gain some of its stats. Damaging a mob with a [[Huntaxes|huntaxe]] deals damage to it until it reaches {{Stat|HP|1}}. Once below {{Stat|HP|10%}}, a Pocket Black Hole can be placed to absorb the mob and gain its [[Attributes|Attribute Shard]].

The {{Attr|Hunter's Fang}} attribute increases the stats gained from the weapons stored in your [[Huntaxes]].<br>The {{Attr|Hunter's Pressure}} attribute increases the speed at which your [[Black Holes]] capture mobs at.

=== Charm Hunting ===
{{Main|Charming}}
Killing a [[Mob]] while any of the [[Charming]] effects are active (like [[Salt]]) grants a small chance to capture their [[Attribute Shard]].

=== Trap Hunting ===
Placing a [[Huntraps|Huntrap]] in a location where mobs have [[Attribute Shard]]s will eventually capture a [[Attribute Shard]].

The {{Attr|Forest Trap}} attribute increases the rate at which your [[Huntraps]] catch Forest Shards.

The {{Attr|Combat Trap}} attribute increases the rate at which your [[Huntraps]] catch Combat Shards.

